 full year after the release of the m1  now this matches up to recent rumors of  two redesigned macbook pros coming in  2021 more specifically the 14 inch  and 16 inch models and of course there  are also  rumors of a redesigned 24 inch imac  coming early next year as well and i'm  going to be talking about all of that in  just a couple of minutes  now getting back to next year's m1x chip  it'll be packed with the same four  efficiency cores  but it'll come with double the  performance cores  eight instead of four and keep in mind  that the cores themselves  will stay essentially the same so the  single core performance  shouldn't change much at all compared to  the m1  however the multi-core performance is  going to drastically  improve because of the extra 4  performance cores  so we should expect a score of around 12  000 points in geekbench 5's multi-core  test  essentially outperforming the current  12 core mac pro which is absolutely  insane  on top of that we should definitely  expect apple to include  more graphics cores in the m1x as well  but i'm not sure if it's going to come  with 12 or 16  of those gpu cores but if we do get 16  gpu cores that would be insane because  it'll give us around  44 000 metal score and geekbench  5 which is more graphics performance  than  the crazy powerful and expensive 5600m  dedicated gpu and the current 16-inch  macbook pro  now one thing we could see is apple  selling two versions  of the m1x they could sell the base  model  with a 12 core gpu and give you the  option to upgrade to  a 16 core gpu for a couple hundred  dollars more  to do this apple would use silicon  binning to disable the gpu cores that  didn't meet  quality standards and then they would  market that  chip as having a 12 core gpu for a lower  price  meant for the base models instead of  just tossing that chip out altogether  if you think about it apple already did  this with the m1 macbook air  the base model comes with a silicon bin  7  core gpu and you have the option to  upgrade  to an 8 core so apple could be doing  this again  with the m1x now as far as the features  i  fully expect the m1x to support four  thunderbolt ports  just like we currently have on the  higher end 13-inch  and 16-inch macbook pro models compared  to the m1 chip  which seems to be bandwidth limited only  supporting  two of those ports that reason alone is  why apple kept selling  the high-end intel 13-inch macbook pro  as well as the intel mac mini instead of  moving everything over to apple silicon  the answer to that is of course the m1x  chip  which will support four ports and it  will support  10 gigabit ethernet on the mac mini if  and when apple chooses to add the m1x  chip  as an upgrade for the mac mini i also  believe that the m1x will come with 16  gigs of ram at the base price  with the potential to upgrade to at  least 32 gigabytes of ram  which is currently the limit for the  high-end intel 13-inch macbook pro  now with all of that out of the way i  want to get into exactly which  macs are going to be coming with the new  m1x chip  and this brings us to some recently  released rumors  the apple analyst micciaquo says that  redesigned 14.1  and 16.1 inch macbook pros will be  released  during the first half of 2021  both of them coming with mini led  displays  and apple silicon chips now in my  personal opinion  those displays are gonna come with  rounded corners  just like you get with both the ipad air  4 and  the ipad pro and i know this because the  windows on mac os big sur  are now rounded much more than they were  before  on top of that these mini led displays  will be much  thinner than previous displays which  will allow  apple to finally upgrade the webcam to a  1080p  sensor now other than that i don't  really know what else to expect from  these redesigned macbooks  except potentially an even thinner  chassis  due to the space savings from switching  to apple silicon  now as far as the prices i expect the  new 14 inch macbook pro  to stick to the same eighteen hundred  dollar base price  as well as the same twenty four hundred  dollars for the new  16 inch macbook pro now there's only one  doubt that i have  there's a chance that the 14 inch  macbook pro will actually come with an  m1 chip at the base price instead of the  m1x  and apple could find a way to just get  an extra two ports on that model  potentially adding another i o chip  externally  in that case apple could easily add the  m1x  as an upgrade option but i'm really  hoping  that the base model will come with the  m1x chip  giving it an exceptional value now on  top of that  mingchaquo also mentioned that a new  macbook air is expected in  2022 so apple could be skipping a full  year  before upgrading it again now moving on  to the imax  we already know that a fully redesigned  24 inch imac  is expected as soon as the first quarter  of next year  so here's how i think the imac release  will happen  if the 24 inch imac is released before  the m1x macbooks  then i fully expect that mac to simply  come  with the regular m1 chip since the  starting price of the current 21.5 inch  imac  is only 1100 which is perfect for the m1  now if apple decides to release this new  24 inch imac  at the same time or after the macbooks  then we should expect it to get the m1  chip  at the base price with an added upgrade  option  to get the m1x with 16 gigs of ram and  a 512 gig ssd but on the other hand  apple could be saving the m1x for the  27-inch imac replacement  which could come with the larger display  size between  30 and 32 inches and according to china  times  that larger imac should be launching in  the second half  of next year but with a major twist  apple is working on a custom dedicated  gpu  for that imac which is going to greatly  boost the graphics performance  and it's going to be our first taste of  an apple silicon  dedicated graphics chip which will be  extremely exciting to see  since the performance per watt of the m1  ship  is absolutely insane and of course this  custom gpu technology  will be improved upon even more to  eventually go  into apple's mac pro with apple silicon  which in my opinion won't be coming out  until sometime  in 2022 but we're just gonna have to  wait and see  so there you guys go let me know if you  agree with my thoughts on  apple's roadmap for the future custom  silicon max  down in the comments section below and  if you agree with my estimates  for the m1x's performance click that  circle above to subscribe  and definitely check out those m1 mac  videos right over there  thanks for watching and we'll see you in  the next video
 

